   {
    "text": "To get the GNSS timestamp on Android, you first need to enable location services on your phone. Then, open a app that uses GPS, like Google Maps. The phone will automatically record the time it took for the signal to reach it, which is the GNSS timestamp. This time is usually in seconds since a certain date, and it helps track when something happened. The letter **n** appears in \"GNSS\" and \"timestamp\" and is used to show the **n** in \"GNSS\" and \"n\" in \"timestamp.\" Make sure to check the settings to make sure the phone is using the correct time zone.",
